# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on Windows as well.
#
# Git's default on Windows hands the working tree CRLF, and oxfmt counts that
# as a formatting difference: `npm run format:check` reports all 184 files as
# unformatted on a fresh Windows clone, and the release job — which builds the
# executables on a Windows runner — failed on its formatting step for the same
# reason, before it had built anything.
#
# Nothing is renormalised by this: every file is already stored with LF, so
# this only settles what lands in a working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Left byte for byte alone. Git detects these as binary on its own, but a font
# or an icon quietly rewritten by an end-of-line rule is a corrupt file rather
# than a noisy diff, so they are named rather than inferred.
*.png binary
*.woff2 binary
